// Truncated rhombicuboctahedral hub with eighteen octagonal socket faces.
// SHAFT occupies the -Y cardinal face; the other seventeen carry OCT-8M ports.
// Six cardinal faces and twelve diagonal faces retain full cube symmetry.
// Eight hexagonal corners and twenty-four small cut faces separate the sockets.
// shaft-diameter must match the shaft for an unscaled link.
// Rim controls the minimum wall border around shaft and diagonal openings.
// corner-inset moves the eight hexagonal faces inward, in metres.
// Socket positions and dimensions stay fixed. The default inset is 1.75 m.
// The spindle continues from SHAFT into the hub; core-diameter must match it.
// Each octagonal mouth has four pipes. Runs follow the walls with round bends.
// pipe-seed selects separate routes through wall and corner lanes.
// Each pipe connects two different exits or ends at the spindle.
// Routes have no branches and reserve clearance for their rounded bends.
// Four rear feeds enter the spindle. Other mouths can use rear wall lanes
// to reach it if their exit routes are blocked.
// The spindle ends in a smaller copy of the hub at the room centre.
// Dark seams follow each polygon edge on the spindle end.
// Pipe feeds have dark spindle flanges and leak marks toward the centre (+Y).
// Eight hexagonal beams connect it to the corner panels. Dark collars mark
// both ends. Pipe routes stay on the corner perimeters, clear of the beams.
// Regions: 0 socket walls, 1 corner panels, 2 tunnel closures, 3 shaft closure,
// 4 dark structural joints, 5 polygon and portal seams, 6 pipes, 7 spindle,
// 8 structural beams, 9 pipe flanges, 10 leak stains.
// Corner panels have one closed hexagonal service cover.
// Wall edges have 0.06 m seams; portal edges have 0.10 m seams.
fn room_parameter_count() -> u32 {
    return prefab_rotor_hub_parameter_count();
}
fn room_parameter(index: u32) -> AssetParameter {
    return prefab_rotor_hub_parameter(index);
}
fn room_parameter_name(index: u32) -> AssetName {
    return prefab_rotor_hub_parameter_name(index);
}
fn room_build(parameters: read AssetValues, asset: mut RoomAsset) -> bool {
    return prefab_rotor_hub_build(read parameters, mut asset);
}
fn room_material_count() -> u32 {
    return prefab_rotor_hub_material_count();
}
fn room_material(region: u32, parameters: read AssetValues) -> PanelMaterial {
    return prefab_rotor_hub_material(region, read parameters);
}
